From 98d7639b8916563d2e6b15a868dbc98f3e96aa96 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yuhangle <893033655@qq.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 21:28:44 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] zram: port multi-compression streams and recompression

Backport of the upstream multi-compression support (v6.2, 2022-11-09
series) plus the recompression machinery, adapted to the 6.1 tree which
already carries the compression backends API:

- zram_drv.h: ZRAM_MAX_COMPS, per-priority comps[]/params[]/comp_algs[],
  slot compression priority encoded in the page flags
  (ZRAM_COMP_PRIORITY_MASK) and the ZRAM_INCOMPRESSIBLE flag
- zram_drv.c: zram_set_priority()/zram_get_priority(), priority aware
  comp_algorithm/algorithm_params/recomp_algorithm sysfs knobs, per
  priority zcomp creation/destruction, priority aware read path
  (zram_read_from_zspool) and the write path always using the primary
  comp
- recompression: zram_recompress() + recompress_store(), so that idle or
  huge pages can be re-compressed with a stronger secondary algorithm
  (echo "algo=zstd priority=1" > recomp_algorithm; echo type=idle >
  recompress), freeing the old zsmalloc handle on success
- Kconfig: ZRAM_MULTI_COMP, enabled in gki_defconfig

Recompression is triggered from user space, as upstream does; idle pages
are selected via the existing IDLE flag (ZRAM_TRACK_ENTRY_ACTIME is not
required).
---
 arch/arm64/configs/gki_defconfig |   1 +
 drivers/block/zram/Kconfig       |   9 +
 drivers/block/zram/zram_drv.c    | 639 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++----
 drivers/block/zram/zram_drv.h    |  23 +-
 4 files changed, 587 insertions(+), 85 deletions(-)

